# Slice 297 probe (REPEATED-DECL-TYPED-RECEPTION, the ordinary reception it reuses): the assignment of a char value to the
# int place z; the program defines no char -> int receiver.  Exit: z's value, 25 for the implicit convert; a refusal at
# translation is the ordinary reception's own answer.
fn: run () int
    ---
        int: z 5
        char: c 6
        z: c
        return: z
        catch: convert ()
            return: 25
    ---
end: run
int: code run()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
